I re-checked it, and the averaging fix is correct. Your colleague was right that it changed one other case, though: `median([])` went from `undefined` to `NaN`. I'd mentioned that last time but didn't fix it. Now empty input returns `undefined` again, as it did before my change.

```js
function median(values) {
  const sorted = [...values].sort((a, b) => a - b);
  if (sorted.length === 0) {
    return undefined;
  }
